.superpowers/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
config.local.json
# Derived, rebuildable, and large (~1MB per symbol of full history): the feature
# panel is a cache of sell_in_may's price cache, keyed by data_hash — never state.
state/panel_cache/
# NOTE state/tmp_gen_*/ is deliberately NOT ignored: an Actions runner is destroyed
# after every session, so committing the in-flight F1 checkpoints is the only way a
# generation that outlives its time budget can resume instead of re-simulating.
# They are removed by the run that finishes the generation.
#
# sell_in_may/config.py makes these two on import, wherever it lives. Vendored, it
# lives here — and the cache arena actually reads is data/cache/, not this.
vendor/sell_in_may/cache/
vendor/sell_in_may/output/
